      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Had this happen yesterday, accidentally joined on some people who wanted to be private. Everyone involved was very shocked this was possible.\n**Example scenario:**\n1. Send an Invite Request\n2. They deny your request\n3. You (accidentally) find which world they are in, and is able to join anyway.\nThe problem is that friends/friends+ instances show up even if **everyone** in an instance is on Orange.\nThe problem is not the implementation of this feature, but because almost no one knows the system works in this way. People will wrongly believe they are fully private when on Orange, which can lead to unexpected invasion of privacy.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
